// @test: A reserved word as a typed parameter name names the word
// @description: `f(match<Int>)` used to fail with the bare "Expected parameter declaration"; the
//   declaration parser now names the reserved word. `ptr<T>` types and
//   `fail<E>(e)` statements are unaffected: only `word<T>` followed by `,` `)` or `=` is refused.
// @category: parser, diagnostics
// @expect: fail
// @expect-error: 'match' is a reserved word and cannot be used as a parameter name

f(match<Int>)<Int> -> { return 1 }
main()<Int> -> { return f(2) }
